+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -uo pipefail
+
+if (( $# < 2 )); then
+  echo "usage: $0 LOG COMMAND [ARG ...]" >&2
+  exit 2
+fi
+
+log=$1
+shift
+
+{
+  printf 'COMMAND:'
+  printf ' %q' "$@"
+  printf '\n'
+  printf 'WORKDIR: %s\n' "$PWD"
+} >"$log"
+
+"$@" > >(tee -a "$log") 2> >(tee -a "$log" >&2)
+status=$?
+printf 'EXIT_STATUS: %d\n' "$status" | tee -a "$log"
+exit "$status"

codex
The fresh non-vacuity mutation parses and compiles successfully. It changes only the symbolic entry postcondition to require the established count plus one; `[11]` satisfies the original precondition but makes that target 2 while both Python implementations return 1. The mutated mutual proof is running now and must fail on the changed obligation—not on parsing or infrastructure—to count as valid evidence.
